        "value": "at risk",
        "source": "elcat-v2024.1",
        "note": "Hawu is primarily used only in the home and in contexts of traditional culture. It is not used for business, education, or travel.\r\n\r\nHawu has complex phonetics, with implosives, phonetically long and short vowels, and lengthened consonants. All this makes the language hard to acquire for many children. \r\n\r\nIntergenerational transmission of specialized traditional knowledge and vocabulary is breaking down. [Endangerment.Certainty: 0.2]",
        "scale": "elcat-v2024.1"
      },
